{"model": "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-Q4_K_M.gguf", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Answer using only the extracted intermediate representation and the question.\nDo not add events. If the representation is insufficient, return UNKNOWN.\n\nIntermediate representation:\n{\n  \"old_state\": \"User is planning a trip to LA, has a standard 9-to-5 job (Mon-Fri), and is organizing a cleaning schedule.\",\n  \"new_state\": \"User intends to book a flight to Thailand next Monday for a six-week trip, working remotely from beach cafes.\",\n  \"change_type\": \"UNKNOWN\",\n  \"status\": \"INFERRED\",\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"Session 7, User turn 1\",\n    \"Session 7, User turn 3\",\n    \"Session 14, User turn 1\"\n  ]\n}\n\nQuestion: I’ve been thinking about booking a flight to Thailand next Monday to spend the next six weeks exploring the islands, just keeping up with my usual daily tasks from my laptop at local beach cafes. Are there any major structural roadblocks stopping me from just packing up and doing this?\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object:\n{\n  \"decision\": \"ANSWER | UNKNOWN\",\n  \"answer\": \"specific current-fact answer or null\",\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\"session/turn references\"]\n}\nIf ANSWER, the answer must state the specific current fact, not only Yes or No.\nIf evidence is insufficient, use UNKNOWN and answer null. Do not invent events."}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "max_tokens": 256, "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}, "stream": false}